Well, like I said in my wizard ascension post, it was time to try
something a little more difficult.  I don't really think tourist
is that difficult though- either that, or I'm finally figuring
out when to run and when to fight.

Anyway- this game was made very easy by the two non-castle wands
of wishing.  There weren't a lot of significant things in this
game other than that.

Asmodeus was a real pain- he somehow acquired a wand of digging,
so I had to track him down about 5 or 6 times before he ran out
of charges.  All the weapons in my bag came from a sac fest at
an alter right above the castle, except for Grimtooth, which was
apparantly randomly generated on one of my victims (is that even
possible?  maybe it was just generated on the floor- I'm not sure).
The magicbane also didn't come naturally- I used one of the wishes
for that- I figured I had plenty...

Orcus didn't have possession of his wand of death when I got to
him- I hit him once and he teleported to the stairs, leaving the
wand behind.  That seemed rather strange.

It took me forever to find Vlad's tower- I ended up digging out
all the walls in two levels before I finally remembered that
I had magic markers and blank scrolls...

The Astral plane was a pain as well- I had to try all three altars,
and since I was wearing a cloak of displacement instead of something
with better cancellation, Death managed to fry me once.  I ended
up just zapping him with a wand of teleport, and he moved left one
square, allowing me to run right by him like the coward that I
am.

My only disappointment with this game was the lack of a wand of
polymorph, and the lack of a big room level.

I hope all of my fellow demigods and demigoddesses enjoy the snacks
that I brought along...

P,W,T down.  many more to go.

